Subject: Fix Cricut Design Space's device helper and Print Then Cut printing under Wine

propsys: add System.Devices.Aep.{CanPair,IsPresent,SignalStrength} and
System.DeviceInterface.Bluetooth.{VendorId,ProductId} to the system property
table. The keys are already defined in include/propkey.h.

windows.devices.enumeration: implement DeviceWatcher add_Removed,
remove_Updated and remove_Removed (they returned E_NOTIMPL) by keeping
handler lists, like add_Added does.

Without these, CricutDevice.exe throws while creating its Bluetooth
DeviceWatcher and exits before it ever opens the USB serial port.

gdiplus: an image with alpha drawn at its own size to a printer that can't
blend (SHADEBLENDCAPS SB_NONE) skipped the software path, so gdi_alpha_blend
fell back to a plain StretchBlt and transparent pixels printed black. Use the
software path there too; it blends onto white, as scaled draws already do.
CricutSystemPrinter.exe draws Print Then Cut pages this way, so the page came
out black around the design and lost its registration marks.

Against Wine 11.0 (stable). Same changes as wine-cricut.patch, rebased; builds but untested at runtime.
Apply from the Wine source root: patch -p1 < wine-11.0-cricut.patch

